mods: jokers-luck, _jokersluck-merge
timeout: 120s
# A second JokersLuck on a unit that already carries one must MERGE (the stacks add up on the one object), the way a
# vanilla LuckUp merges, under both apply_status context shapes (docs/engine-map.md "Status effects"):
#  - a Component ctx (the passive component): _jokersluck-merge gives every player cat StatusOnBattleStart
#    { JokersLuck 1 JokersLuck 2 } -> one JokersLuck with 3 stacks on each cat;
#  - the Character ctx (StatusOnSpawnIn, mid-fight): JokersLuckRat gets the same pair on spawn -> one JokersLuck with
#    3 stacks on "Lil' Rat".
# Before the fix both units carried TWO JokersLuck objects (1 and 2): the merge lookup walked ctx+0x20, which is the
# Scene in both shapes, not the unit. No _autoplay: the fight waits on the player, so no turn reroll changes stacks
# (OBSERVED with seed 42: the first cat's JokersLuck is still unrolled after `wait turns 1`).
wait frames 120
seed 42
enter TacticsTest
wait turns 1
dump
expect stacks JokersLuck on 0 == 3
expect stacks JokersLuck on 3 == 3
cmd spawn JokersLuckRat
expect console "Spawned JokersLuckRat" within 10
wait frames 30
dump
expect stacks JokersLuck on "Lil' Rat" == 3
quit
